% === provenance: McCabe1976 ===
% CLAIM: Cyclomatic complexity is defined graph-theoretically as v(G)=e-n+p (e-n+2p for
%   a program graph), and for a structured program equals the number of predicates plus
%   one; compound predicates count once per condition.
% FOUND-VIA: scholar search "cyclomatic complexity measure control flow graph"
