%   http://www.literateprogramming.com/mccabe.pdf)
% PICKED: the original primary source defining the measure; the derived "decision
%   points + 1" rule and the compound-predicate rule are both stated by McCabe himself,
%   which is exactly what the implementation's counting rules must rest on.
% QUOTE (p.308, Definition 1): "The cyclomatic number V(G) of a graph G with n vertices,
%   e edges, and p connected components is v(G) = e - n + p."
% QUOTE (p.315): "the cyclomatic complexity of a structured program equals the number of
%   predicates plus one" ... "In practice compound predicates such as IF 'c1 AND c2' THEN
%   are treated as contributing two to complexity since without the connective AND we
%   would have IF c1 THEN IF c2 THEN which has two predicates."
% VERIFIED: full-text PDF read (13pp, pdftotext); the second quote directly licenses the
%   +1-per-boolean-operator rule that radon implements and learnlog will replicate.
% COUNTER: scholar search 'TS=("cyclomatic complexity" AND (critique OR criticism OR
%   "empirical validation" OR invalid))' -p wos -l 10 -- surfaced Shepperd1988,
%   ShepperdInce1994, Landman2016, VinjuGodfrey2012.  The DEFINITION is not disputed;
%   what is disputed is its validity as a complexity/maintainability proxy.  Claim is
%   therefore stated as a definition only, and the validity critiques are cited
%   separately (see Shepperd1988, Landman2016).
% DATE: 2026-08-31
